# LF in the repository and the working tree on every OS, whatever core.autocrlf
# says: a native checkout leaves the tree half CRLF (git) and half LF (editors,
# xtask), and a CRLF script run on Linux dies as `/bin/sh^M: bad interpreter`.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.rs text
*.toml text
*.md text
*.qml text
*.yml text
*.yaml text
*.ps1 text
*.sh text eol=lf

# Captured raw git output for parser tests: byte-exact, never re-encoded.
*.bin binary
